# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Perform explicit noise learning for PEA and PEC {#perform-explicit-noise-learning-for-pea-and-pec}"
msgstr "Realizar aprendizaje de ruido explícito para PEA y PEC {#perform-explicit-noise-learning-for-pea-and-pec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The new Estimator no longer performs *implicit* noise learning when the PEA or PEC error\n"
"mitigation method is selected. You must learn the noise models explicitly and pass them\n"
"in. Use the new [`NoiseLearnerV3`](/guides/noise-learning#noiselearnerv3) to control how circuits\n"
"are stratified into layers. It takes a list of boxed circuit instructions (for example,\n"
"the unique layers) as input.\n"
msgstr ""
"El nuevo Estimator ya no realiza aprendizaje de ruido *implícito* cuando se selecciona el método de\n"
"mitigación de errores PEA o PEC. Debes aprender los modelos de ruido de forma explícita y\n"
"pasarlos. Usa el nuevo [`NoiseLearnerV3`](/guides/noise-learning#noiselearnerv3) para controlar cómo se\n"
"estratifican los circuitos en capas. Toma como entrada una lista de instrucciones de circuito en cajas (por ejemplo,\n"
"las capas únicas).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important\">\n"
"PEA and PEC now **require** this explicit pattern. Do not skip the noise-learning step\n"
"or your code will fail. Measurement noise learning for TREX is unaffected and continues to work as before.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Importante\">\n"
"PEA y PEC ahora **requieren** este patrón explícito. No omitas el paso de aprendizaje de ruido\n"
"o tu código fallará. El aprendizaje de ruido de medición para TREX no se ve afectado y sigue funcionando como antes.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, if your code uses `NoiseLearner` and passes the resulting noise model to server-side Estimator, you need to [migrate to `NoiseLearnerV3`](/guides/migrate-to-noise-learner-v3). Do NOT use the older `NoiseLearner`, which is incompatible with the new Estimator.\n"
msgstr "Del mismo modo, si tu código usa `NoiseLearner` y pasa el modelo de ruido resultante al Estimator del lado del servidor, necesitas [migrar a `NoiseLearnerV3`](/guides/migrate-to-noise-learner-v3). NO uses el `NoiseLearner` anterior, que es incompatible con el nuevo Estimator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All of the noise learning options in the server-side Estimator (`LayerNoiseLearningOptions`) map directly to the `NoiseLearnerV3` option ([`NoiseLearnerV3Options`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-noise-learner-v3-options)), with the exception of `max_layers_to_learn`. The number of layers to learn is instead based on the number of layers passed to `NoiseLearnerV3`.\n"
msgstr "Todas las opciones de aprendizaje de ruido en el Estimator del lado del servidor (`LayerNoiseLearningOptions`) se corresponden directamente con la opción de `NoiseLearnerV3` ([`NoiseLearnerV3Options`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-noise-learner-v3-options)), con la excepción de `max_layers_to_learn`. El número de capas a aprender se basa, en cambio, en el número de capas pasadas a `NoiseLearnerV3`.\n"

